# Build output.
/target/

# The mutation gate's configuration and state are **not** here, and not by accident.
#
# The intent is that this machine's global gitignore (`~/.config/git/ignore`) excludes
# `noha.yaml`, `.noha/` and `AGENTS.md` from every repository on it, under the heading "local
# verification toolchain — never commit, in any repository on this machine". That is policy, and a
# `!noha.yaml` negation in this file would outrank it — which is exactly why there is not one.
#
# **Checked 2026-08-25: the policy was described here and was not in that file.** It held two
# `.claude/settings.local.json` lines and nothing else, `core.excludesfile` was unset, and all
# three paths came back from `git check-ignore` as NOT IGNORED — one `git add -A` from being
# committed, with this comment standing over them saying they could not be. A comment that
# asserts a safety net is not a safety net.
#
# So: `git check-ignore -v noha.yaml .noha/ AGENTS.md` before believing this paragraph. It costs
# nothing and it is the only thing here that is evidence rather than intent.
#
# `AGENTS.md` belongs on that list for a second reason. `noha init` writes it, and it links to
# `.noha/INTEGRITY_PROMPT.md` — so committing it would publish a document pointing at a file no
# clone has, which is the mistake `git log` records as "a public doc linking to a private item".
#
# **The price, stated rather than worked around:** `tests/integrity.rs` reads `noha.yaml`, so a
# fresh clone cannot run it, and the mutation gate's source list cannot be reviewed from the
# repository. `README.md` says so where it describes the gate. The list lives beside the tree; ask
# for it rather than assuming a clone is missing something.
#
# The scratch below is ignored on its own account, for anyone who does have the files locally.
.noha/work/
.noha/tmp/

# A memory store belonging to an MCP server that happens to run in this directory. Not part of the
# project, and its lock file is held open for as long as that server lives — which is also why
# `noha prober` cannot walk this tree while the server is running.
mnema.store
mnema.store.key
mnema.store.lock

# The demo is its own workspace and builds into its own target directory. Deleting `demo/` makes
# this line dead, which is the intended shape.
/demo/target/
